Z||000007||theogre||08-20-2001||10:20 PM||||Details on U.S. copyright can be found at <A HREF="http://www.loc.gov" TARGET=_blank>www.loc.gov</A> <P>A race team, company, etc, name is usually a trademark. In the U.S. that's handled by the Patent Office. <A HREF="http://www.uspto.gov" TARGET=_blank>www.uspto.gov</A> <P>Registering documents for copyright is insurance if someone rips you off. It's not required or hidiously expensive.<P>Regiserting a trade mark on the other hand is rather expensive. If I read all that right,,, it's about a $1000 in upfront costs and there are renewal fees as well.<P>If you are sure you will not be conducting national/international business, you can contact your local prothonitary(I'm not sure of spelling at the momnet.) and register a local "DBA" (Doing Business As). This is sort of a city/state thing. It's much less expensive.||||reg||1
